  "title": "Removing a field or subrecord from a record moves PGM by 1 as well as RDM",
  "statement": "A record save that leaves out a field or subrecord the record had bumps PSVERSION and PSLOCK PGM by one, besides RDM and SYS, though no component row changes. In the record-save captures PGM moved in exactly the four saves that removed a field (by the record's field set before and after, not the ROWID diff) and in none of the 40 others, inserts included. A record rename moves PGM among many counters; a record delete does not move it.",
